' Arco3D non-destructive Construction Stack (RFC-0049 Section 7.2, implementation step 4).
'
' Depends on arco3d_scene.abas (Vec3, Mesh, Face, Component) -- imported below, so any script that
' imports this file gets the scene object model transitively (confirmed: legacy #IMPORT behaves
' like textual inclusion into one shared global scope, not an isolated module -- there is no
' MODULE/EXPORT support in this toolchain yet).
'
' Scope for this increment:
'   - The stack machinery itself: an ordered list of operations, each independently enabled/
'     disabled, reorderable, editable, and duplicable (RFC-0049 Section 7.2's own MUST list),
'     evaluated non-destructively (BaseMesh is never mutated by Evaluate()), plus an explicit
'     Commit() that is the ONLY way geometry gets destructively baked.
'   - Two real operations to prove the stack end-to-end: MirrorOp (reflect + optional seam weld)
'     and ArrayOp (linear repeat). Both are genuinely non-destructive: each Apply() call takes an
'     input Mesh and returns a brand new Mesh, never mutating its input.
' Deliberately NOT in this increment (bigger, separate algorithms -- topology-aware mesh editing,
' not just whole-mesh transforms like Mirror/Array):
'   - Extrude, Inset, Bevel, cutting/Subdivision (RFC-0049 Section 7.1/7.2's "Extrusion Group",
'     "Bevel", "Subdivision" stack nodes). These need real edge/half-edge topology tracking that
'     Mesh doesn't have yet; adding them here would either be fake or a much bigger increment.
'   - Snapping/alignment (RFC-0049 Section 7.1) -- viewport/interaction concerns, not stack ops.
'
' Known simplification: there is no dirty-tracking/observer system. Mutating an operation's field
' directly (e.g. `op.Enabled = FALSE`) does not auto-recompute anything -- the owning Component's
' RefreshFromStack() (or ConstructionStack.Evaluate() directly) must be called again afterward.
' This is a pull-based, not reactive, evaluation model for now.

#IMPORT "arco3d_scene"

' Documents the contract every construction operation follows. Interfaces in this toolchain only
' validate methods, not fields -- Enabled/Id/Clone() are a convention every op below still follows,
' checked by the smoke test, not by the language itself.
INTERFACE ConstructionOp
    FUNCTION Apply(inputMesh AS Mesh) AS Mesh
END INTERFACE

' Negates the chosen local axis of a point. Nested IF/ELSE only -- this dialect has no ELSEIF.
FUNCTION MirrorVertex(vertex AS Vec3, axis AS String) AS Vec3
    IF axis == "X" THEN
        RETURN Vec3(0 - vertex.X, vertex.Y, vertex.Z)
    ELSE
        IF axis == "Y" THEN
            RETURN Vec3(vertex.X, 0 - vertex.Y, vertex.Z)
        ELSE
            RETURN Vec3(vertex.X, vertex.Y, 0 - vertex.Z)
        END IF
    END IF
END FUNCTION

' Linear scan for a vertex within `tolerance` of `target`. Mesh sizes here are small (primitive-
' scale), so O(n) per query / O(n^2) per weld pass is an acceptable, simple starting point -- not
' something a real production mesh editor would keep doing once meshes get large.
FUNCTION FindNearVertexIndex(vertexList AS Array, target AS Vec3, tolerance AS Number) AS Number
    FOR i IN Range(LEN(vertexList))
        candidate = vertexList[i]
        isNear = candidate.EqualsApprox(target, tolerance)
        IF isNear THEN
            RETURN i
        END IF
    NEXT
    RETURN -1
END FUNCTION

' Reflects a mesh across a local axis plane through the origin and appends the mirrored half to
' the original (RFC-0049 Section 7.2's own "Mirror" stack-node example). With Weld enabled (the
' default), seam vertices within WeldTolerance of an existing vertex are reused rather than
' duplicated. Mirrored faces have their winding reversed (index 1 and 2 swapped) because a
' reflection inverts triangle handedness -- without this every mirrored face would point inward.
CLASS MirrorOp IMPLEMENTS ConstructionOp
    Id AS String = ""
    Enabled AS Boolean = TRUE
    Axis AS String = "X"
    Weld AS Boolean = TRUE
    WeldTolerance AS Number = 0.0001

    CONSTRUCTOR(axis AS String = "X", weld AS Boolean = TRUE)
        SELF.Id = ArcoId.Issue("op")
        SELF.Axis = axis
        SELF.Weld = weld
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION Apply(inputMesh AS Mesh) AS Mesh
        axis = SELF.Axis
        weld = SELF.Weld
        tolerance = SELF.WeldTolerance

        outputVertices = []
        FOR vertex IN inputMesh.Vertices
            ignoredPush = Array.Add(outputVertices, vertex.Clone())
        NEXT

        ' remap[i] is the final output-vertex index standing in for input vertex i's mirrored copy
        ' (either a freshly appended vertex, or a weld onto an existing one).
        remap = []
        FOR sourceVertex IN inputMesh.Vertices
            mirrored = MirrorVertex(sourceVertex, axis)
            foundIndex = -1
            IF weld THEN
                foundIndex = FindNearVertexIndex(outputVertices, mirrored, tolerance)
            END IF
            IF foundIndex >= 0 THEN
                ignoredPush = Array.Add(remap, foundIndex)
            ELSE
                ignoredPush = Array.Add(outputVertices, mirrored)
                newIndex = LEN(outputVertices) - 1
                ignoredPush = Array.Add(remap, newIndex)
            END IF
        NEXT

        outputFaces = []
        FOR face IN inputMesh.Faces
            indices = face.Indices
            ignoredPush = Array.Add(outputFaces, Face(indices[0], indices[1], indices[2]))
        NEXT
        FOR face IN inputMesh.Faces
            indices = face.Indices
            a = remap[indices[0]]
            b = remap[indices[1]]
            c = remap[indices[2]]
            ' Swap b/c: reverses winding to correct for the reflection's handedness flip.
            ignoredPush = Array.Add(outputFaces, Face(a, c, b))
        NEXT

        outputMesh = Mesh()
        outputMesh.Vertices = outputVertices
        outputMesh.Faces = outputFaces
        outputMesh.RecomputeFaceNormals()
        RETURN outputMesh
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Clone() AS MirrorOp
        copy = MirrorOp(SELF.Axis, SELF.Weld)
        copy.Enabled = SELF.Enabled
        copy.WeldTolerance = SELF.WeldTolerance
        RETURN copy
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' Repeats the input mesh `Count` times (including the unshifted original at index 0), each copy
' shifted by an additional Offset. No welding -- array copies are not generally expected to touch.
CLASS ArrayOp IMPLEMENTS ConstructionOp
    Id AS String = ""
    Enabled AS Boolean = TRUE
    Count AS Number = 2
    Offset AS Vec3 = Vec3(1, 0, 0)

    CONSTRUCTOR(count AS Number = 2, offsetX AS Number = 1, offsetY AS Number = 0, offsetZ AS Number = 0)
        SELF.Id = ArcoId.Issue("op")
        SELF.Count = count
        SELF.Offset = Vec3(offsetX, offsetY, offsetZ)
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION Apply(inputMesh AS Mesh) AS Mesh
        copies = SELF.Count
        IF copies < 1 THEN
            copies = 1
        END IF
        offset = SELF.Offset
        vertexCountPerCopy = LEN(inputMesh.Vertices)

        outputVertices = []
        outputFaces = []
        FOR copyIndex IN Range(copies)
            shift = offset.Scaled(copyIndex)
            FOR vertex IN inputMesh.Vertices
                shifted = vertex.Plus(shift)
                ignoredPush = Array.Add(outputVertices, shifted)
            NEXT
            indexBase = copyIndex * vertexCountPerCopy
            FOR face IN inputMesh.Faces
                indices = face.Indices
                a = indices[0] + indexBase
                b = indices[1] + indexBase
                c = indices[2] + indexBase
                ignoredPush = Array.Add(outputFaces, Face(a, b, c))
            NEXT
        NEXT

        outputMesh = Mesh()
        outputMesh.Vertices = outputVertices
        outputMesh.Faces = outputFaces
        outputMesh.RecomputeFaceNormals()
        RETURN outputMesh
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Clone() AS ArrayOp
        offset = SELF.Offset
        copy = ArrayOp(SELF.Count, offset.X, offset.Y, offset.Z)
        copy.Enabled = SELF.Enabled
        RETURN copy
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' An ordered, non-destructively evaluated list of operations over a base mesh. Evaluate() never
' mutates BaseMesh or any operation; Commit() is the sole, explicit, destructive bake (RFC-0049
' Section 7.2: "The user MUST NOT be forced to destructively commit geometry merely to preview
' later refinement").
CLASS ConstructionStack
    BaseMesh AS Mesh = NULL
    Operations AS Array = []

    CONSTRUCTOR(baseMesh AS Mesh = NULL)
        SELF.BaseMesh = baseMesh
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION AddOperation(operation)
        operations = SELF.Operations
        ignoredPush = Array.Add(operations, operation)
    END FUNCTION

    ' Swaps the operation at `index` with its neighbor in `direction` (-1 earlier, +1 later).
    ' Returns FALSE (no change) if `index` or the resulting position is out of range.
    FUNCTION MoveOperation(index AS Number, direction AS Number) AS Boolean
        operations = SELF.Operations
        count = LEN(operations)
        targetIndex = index + direction
        IF index < 0 THEN
            RETURN FALSE
        END IF
        IF index >= count THEN
            RETURN FALSE
        END IF
        IF targetIndex < 0 THEN
            RETURN FALSE
        END IF
        IF targetIndex >= count THEN
            RETURN FALSE
        END IF
        moving = operations[index]
        displaced = operations[targetIndex]
        operations[index] = displaced
        operations[targetIndex] = moving
        RETURN TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION RemoveOperationAt(index AS Number) AS Boolean
        operations = SELF.Operations
        count = LEN(operations)
        IF index < 0 THEN
            RETURN FALSE
        END IF
        IF index >= count THEN
            RETURN FALSE
        END IF
        ignoredRemoved = Array.RemoveAt(operations, index)
        RETURN TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    ' Runs every enabled operation in order over a clone of BaseMesh. BaseMesh, and every
    ' operation's own parameters, are left untouched -- calling this repeatedly (e.g. after toggling
    ' one operation's Enabled flag) always recomputes from scratch rather than incrementally.
    FUNCTION Evaluate() AS Mesh
        baseMesh = SELF.BaseMesh
        current = baseMesh.Clone()
        operations = SELF.Operations
        FOR operation IN operations
            enabled = operation.Enabled
            IF enabled THEN
                current = operation.Apply(current)
            END IF
        NEXT
        RETURN current
    END FUNCTION

    ' The only destructive operation: bakes the current evaluated result as the new BaseMesh and
    ' clears the operation list. Ordinary Evaluate() calls never do this implicitly.
    FUNCTION Commit()
        evaluated = SELF.Evaluate()
        SELF.BaseMesh = evaluated
        SELF.Operations = []
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Clone() AS ConstructionStack
        baseMesh = SELF.BaseMesh
        clonedBase = baseMesh.Clone()
        copy = ConstructionStack(clonedBase)
        operations = SELF.Operations
        FOR operation IN operations
            ignoredPush = Array.Add(copy.Operations, operation.Clone())
        NEXT
        RETURN copy
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

' ---- Component integration --------------------------------------------------------------------
'
' Component.Stack (declared in arco3d_scene.abas) is deliberately untyped there, since that file
' cannot name ConstructionStack without a circular dependency. These three functions are the real
' entry points for giving a component a construction stack; a plain CreateBlock()/CreateWedge()/
' etc. Component has Stack == NULL until AttachConstructionStack() is called on it.

' Wraps a component's current LocalMesh (cloned, so later edits to the component's live mesh don't
' alias the stack's own BaseMesh) in a fresh ConstructionStack and attaches it. Returns the stack.
FUNCTION AttachConstructionStack(component AS Component) AS ConstructionStack
    localMesh = component.LocalMesh
    clonedMesh = localMesh.Clone()
    stack = ConstructionStack(clonedMesh)
    component.Stack = stack
    RETURN stack
END FUNCTION

' Appends `operation` to component.Stack and immediately refreshes LocalMesh from it. Requires
' AttachConstructionStack() to have been called first.
FUNCTION AddConstructionOp(component AS Component, operation)
    stack = component.Stack
    stack.AddOperation(operation)
    RefreshComponentFromStack(component)
END FUNCTION

' Recomputes component.LocalMesh from component.Stack.Evaluate(). Call this after directly
' mutating an operation's fields (e.g. `op.Enabled = FALSE`) or reordering/removing operations --
' there is no automatic dirty-tracking (see module header).
FUNCTION RefreshComponentFromStack(component AS Component)
    stack = component.Stack
    component.LocalMesh = stack.Evaluate()
END FUNCTION
